WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:03.857
Hi everyone, my name is Iman. Today I want to give you a

00:03.857 --> 00:07.455
demo of Thursday prototype of an agent that you can control

00:07.455 --> 00:10.633
just through your voice and that you can use to both

00:10.633 --> 00:13.571
control your operating system as well as writing

00:13.571 --> 00:17.420
applications. Thursday, are you with us?

00:17.420 --> 00:20.445
Yeah, come here ready to help with whatever is on your

00:20.445 --> 00:21.860
screen.

00:21.860 --> 00:27.210
Now I would really like you to bring up the Calculator app.

00:27.210 --> 00:29.220
On it.

00:29.220 --> 00:34.530
Now calculator is open. Please calculate 5 + 5.

00:35.070 --> 00:37.850
One SEC.

00:47.480 --> 00:49.770
5 + 5 is 10.

00:49.770 --> 00:52.223
Thank you for confirming this. Can you switch back to

00:52.223 --> 00:54.720
Safari please?

00:54.720 --> 00:56.930
Switching back now.

00:56.930 --> 01:00.547
So you can see that you can see that the agent is able to

01:00.547 --> 01:04.288
control the operating system. It actually cascades down the

01:04.288 --> 01:07.594
commands. There is a fast session and then that fast

01:07.594 --> 01:11.211
session is built using GPD 5.6 Lunar. So it's really fast

01:11.211 --> 01:14.890
for like single commands that you just saw. And then there

01:14.890 --> 01:18.507
is a deep session that you can use for more complex tasks

01:18.507 --> 01:22.062
that will run in the background. And the real time model

01:22.062 --> 01:25.555
will actually be notified whenever there is a new event

01:25.555 --> 01:26.900
from both sessions.

01:26.900 --> 01:30.592
So can you quickly build an open street map? Demo

01:30.592 --> 01:34.802
application can be done in a single file of the top five

01:34.802 --> 01:38.840
points of interest on Crete.

01:38.840 --> 01:42.830
Sure, I'll put that together.

01:42.840 --> 01:45.422
Now while this is building that single file demo in the

01:45.422 --> 01:46.780
background.

01:46.780 --> 01:51.760
All right, writing the HTML file now.

01:55.740 --> 01:58.463
Now, while this is building, can you bring up tomorrow's

01:58.463 --> 02:01.460
weather in a new window?

02:01.460 --> 02:03.440
Sure, checking.

02:03.440 --> 02:06.570
OK, tomorrow's Weather for Crete is open in a new Safari

02:06.570 --> 02:07.610
tab.

02:07.610 --> 02:10.530
Please switch to it.

02:10.710 --> 02:13.490
Switching now.

02:14.440 --> 02:18.223
Alright, I'm on the weather tab and the demo file is still

02:18.223 --> 02:20.330
